.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:* `concatFn`: Concatenation of `r` codewords into a single string.
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:The proof uses a counting argument: the `r`-th power of the Kraft sum counts concatenations of
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:`r` codewords, weighted by length. Since the code is uniquely decodable, these concatenations are
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:section concatFn
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:private def concatFn (w : Fin r → S) : List α :=
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:private lemma concatFn_length {w : Fin r → S} :
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:    (concatFn w).length = ∑ i : Fin r, (w i).val.length := by
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:  simp [List.sum_ofFn, concatFn]
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:end concatFn
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:/-- For uniquely decodable codes, the concatenation map is injective.
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:This is the key property: distinct tuples of codewords produce distinct concatenations. -/
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:private lemma concatFn_injective_of_uniquelyDecodable {S : Finset (List α)}
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:    Function.Injective (concatFn (S := S) (r := r)) := by
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:/-- Length of a concatenation of `r` codewords lies in `[r, r*sup length]`
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:private lemma concatFn_length_mem_Icc {S : Finset (List α)}
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:    (concatFn w).length ∈ Finset.Icc r (r * S.sup List.length) := by
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:  rw [concatFn_length, Finset.mem_Icc]
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:  -- We use maxLen to bound lengths of `r`-fold concatenations.
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:  -- Let `T` be the set of all concatenations of `r` codewords from `S`.
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:  let T : Finset (List α) := Finset.image concatFn (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin r → S))
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:  -- Any `x ∈ T` is a concatenation of `r` nonempty codewords, hence `r ≤ |x| ≤ r*maxLen`.
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:    exact concatFn_length_mem_Icc
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:  -- each tuple contributes the weight `(1/D)^{|concatFn w|}`.
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:    -- Each tuple contributes the weight `(1/D)^{|concatFn w|}`.
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:    _ = ∑ w, (1 / D) ^ (concatFn w).length := by
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:      simpa [concatFn_length] using Finset.prod_pow_eq_pow_sum Finset.univ _ _
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:    -- Unique decodability makes `concatFn` injective, so these concatenations are distinct;
.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/InformationTheory/Coding/KraftMcMillan.lean:        (fun _ _ _ _ hEq => concatFn_injective_of_uniquelyDecodable h r hEq)).symm
